WEBVTT

00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:15,300
thoughts on the zyto scans that many acupuncturists said nutritionists are running these days are

00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:24,900
they accurate and identified bacteria and viruses. I'd say yes and no so that I think they're

00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:33,220
beneficial on the frequency scans can be beneficial to identify that a person may have a bacteria

00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:38,740
or a virus, but I've always said they are not something that you would quote unquote

00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:50,020
diagnose off of. So if it's another test, for instance, if I run a CBC and I have an elevated

00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:55,860
white blood cell code and I didn't have an elevated white blood cell code in my previous CBCs,

00:00:56,660 --> 00:01:02,980
then I could say that there's a high likelihood that I have an infection. That I would compare that

00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:09,300
with the differential of the complete blood count. If my neutrophils were elevated and my lymphocytes

00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:13,220
were suppressed, I'd say that it's a pretty good chance that it's a bacterial infection.

00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:18,340
If that was reversed, my lymphocytes were elevated, my neutrophils were suppressed,

00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:26,260
and it's a pretty good chance that it's a viral infection. But can I just run a zyto scan to know

00:01:26,340 --> 00:01:34,180
if it's a bacteria or a virus? It will give you clues. I think a blood test is going to give you

00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:40,660
more accurate clues. Remember, a zyto scan is picking up frequencies, and it's picking up frequencies

00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:48,740
quite quickly. So there could be a lot of errors in that as well. My argument against the scans is

00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:54,580
when practitioners use it and tell people you have Lyme disease or you have this disease.

00:01:55,940 --> 00:02:03,860
I think that's dangerous. I don't think it's accurate. I don't think it's proper medicine. I think

00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:10,980
that's, is it mild practice? Any more than some of the things that the medical doctor says,

00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:18,500
I don't think you can just diagnose based upon just one test of anything. All your tests give you

00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:26,500
clues. Yes. If you came up high in, let's say you came up positive online on a zyto scan.

00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:31,300
Does that mean you have Lyme? In my book? No. It doesn't mean you have Lyme. Does it mean that you

00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:39,780
could have bacteria and or viruses? Yes. If you came up very high in multiple bacterias and they gave

00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:45,460
you the name of the bacteria when I diagnosed it and said, this is the exact bacteria that you have

00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:50,420
based upon this zyto scan. I would say no, but is there a greater chance that you may have a

00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:59,380
bacterial infection? Yes, but you'd compare it with other labs too. If your CBC was normal,

00:02:59,380 --> 00:03:07,140
your white blood cell, let's say, was 4.5. And your neutrophils in the facites were within normal

00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:15,780
range too, but then you showed high bacteria on a zyto scan. I would doubt that that was accurate.

00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:21,620
Is there anything wrong with doing some treatment on the right based upon the zyto scan? Absolutely not.

00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:27,620
It's not going to be invasive. Nothing like that. Would you use an antibiotic based upon a positive

00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:32,820
bacteria on a zyto scan? No, I wouldn't because that's going to be more invasive. So,

00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:40,900
long story short, any test that you do, it has imperfections. Nothing is going to be perfect gold

00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:48,500
standard. So, you use a test wisely to give you clues. So, your run as a zyto scan, you came up

00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:53,860
positive for virus. Let's say, Epstein-Barr virus. Does that mean that you have Epstein-Barr virus?

00:03:53,860 --> 00:04:00,260
I would say no, it doesn't. You would look at other tests as well. If your white blood cell count

00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:06,820
again was within normal range and your lymphocyte count was within normal range, this zyto scan could have

00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:16,020
been picking up a past Epstein-Barr virus. Most of us have latent Epstein-Barr virus. If you did an

00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:23,620
IgG antibody test for Epstein-Barr virus, probably eight out of ten people would show positive and yet

00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:30,500
not have any signs of current Epstein-Barr virus because almost everybody has been exposed to

00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:37,460
Epstein-Barr virus. So, like I said, then the zyto scan picks it up and then people run with that say,

00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:42,020
you have Epstein-Barr virus. That's your problem and we need to treat for this. So, they go in a whole

00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:50,260
treatment program for that and it's not accurate. So, I would just be careful using any test as your

00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:58,660
gold standard. Use every test as giving you clues and guiding your treatment and so there's

00:04:58,660 --> 00:05:08,660
nothing wrong with using it if you just use it wisely with that understanding.

